  "loose": {
    "text": [
      {
        "said": "Hi there. This issue is about tools that do one thing well. Small tools are not lesser tools. They are the ones that fit your hand on the first try: the ladle that pours without dripping, the pencil that starts every list, the app with exactly one screen. This week's essay visits three workshops and asks each maker which object they would save from a fire. Nobody picked the expensive one. Also inside: a lamp you can repair with a coin, and a short list of things that got better when someone removed a feature. Until next week, Mara",
        "type": 10
      }
    ],
